{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25146326",
      "title": "Building NextJS Apps: Your Options",
      "lectureOrder": 383,
      "videoOrder": 353,
      "sourceHash": "2137699c216c478bb6f21b3540f82a1dfbdf7c880af0229e494fb46288ba1e8c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.09,
          "end": 4.37,
          "en": "Now before we get our hands dirty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.37,
          "end": 7.26,
          "en": "let's understand deployment in theory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.26,
          "end": 10.42,
          "en": "And let's start with the different deployment options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.42,
          "end": 12.67,
          "en": "Next.js gives you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.67,
          "end": 14.34,
          "en": "Because it turns out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.34,
          "end": 17.99,
          "en": "that you have two totally different ways of building",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.99,
          "end": 21.12,
          "en": "and deploying your Next.js app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.12,
          "end": 25.7,
          "en": "The first and most common option is the Standard Build,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.7,
          "end": 27.81,
          "en": "as I like to call it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.81,
          "end": 31.95,
          "en": "But we also can actually do a Full Static Build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.95,
          "end": 36.67,
          "en": "and deploy our site as a full static website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.67,
          "end": 39.253,
          "en": "Now, let me explain what these two options mean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.16,
          "end": 44.73,
          "en": "You do a standard build by running the next build command",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.73,
          "end": 49.09,
          "en": "or in your project, where you have a package.json file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.09,
          "end": 53.97,
          "en": "this build script which runs next build under the hood.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.97,
          "end": 56.81,
          "en": "We saw that command in action earlier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.81,
          "end": 58.18,
          "en": "in the course already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.18,
          "end": 62.01,
          "en": "when we talked about static page generation and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.01,
          "end": 64.23,
          "en": "When running this command,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.23,
          "end": 69.1,
          "en": "Next.js produces a optimized production build,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.1,
          "end": 72.76,
          "en": "optimized production bundles for your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.76,
          "end": 77.76,
          "en": "and very important, it spits out a service-side application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.41,
          "end": 81.13,
          "en": "The result of running next build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.13,
          "end": 86.13,
          "en": "is an output that requires a NodeJS server to run it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 87.17,
          "end": 91.05,
          "en": "So you can't take the output of next build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 91.05,
          "end": 94.07,
          "en": "and put it onto some static host.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 94.07,
          "end": 98.28,
          "en": "You would be able to do that for a standard React app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 98.28,
          "end": 102.65,
          "en": "a non Next.js app, but because Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 102.65,
          "end": 106.18,
          "en": "has these built-in service-side capabilities,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 106.18,
          "end": 109.95,
          "en": "like pre-rendering pages on the fly, on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 109.95,
          "end": 112.93,
          "en": "revalidating pages, API routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 112.93,
          "end": 115.87,
          "en": "Because it has these service-side features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 115.87,
          "end": 120.21,
          "en": "it needs a NodeJS server to run that code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 120.21,
          "end": 121.42,
          "en": "should make sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 121.42,
          "end": 122.97,
          "en": "Now don't get me wrong,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 122.97,
          "end": 125.38,
          "en": "pages will still be pre-rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 125.38,
          "end": 128.12,
          "en": "during the build process if possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 128.12,
          "end": 131.97,
          "en": "So if you have pages with get static props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.97,
          "end": 134.05,
          "en": "or with no data at all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 134.05,
          "end": 138.97,
          "en": "those pages will still be prebuilt when you run next build.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.97,
          "end": 142.74,
          "en": "But you still have the NodeJS server, as I just explained,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 142.74,
          "end": 144.56,
          "en": "for your API routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.56,
          "end": 147.623,
          "en": "which can and should only run on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.623,
          "end": 149.51,
          "en": "for server-side pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.51,
          "end": 153.01,
          "en": "that use the get server-side props function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.01,
          "end": 155.77,
          "en": "and for page revalidations,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.77,
          "end": 157.36,
          "en": "which you might wanna perform",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 157.36,
          "end": 160.81,
          "en": "on your statically rendered pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.81,
          "end": 165.769,
          "en": "You also need a NodeJS server for dynamic pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.769,
          "end": 170.44,
          "en": "with getStaticPaths if you have fallback set to true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.44,
          "end": 175.44,
          "en": "or blocking, because then some of the pages will be created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 175.45,
          "end": 179.34,
          "en": "on the fly when requests are reaching the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 179.34,
          "end": 182.02,
          "en": "And you need a server that is able to do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 182.02,
          "end": 183.6,
          "en": "for that as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 183.6,
          "end": 187.02,
          "en": "So that is why you need a NodeJS server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 187.02,
          "end": 191.27,
          "en": "for running the output next build gives you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 191.27,
          "end": 193.09,
          "en": "And that has implications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 193.09,
          "end": 196.07999999999998,
          "en": "It means that when you deploy that output,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 196.07999999999998,
          "end": 198.91,
          "en": "you need to deploy it onto a host",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 198.91,
          "end": 201.73,
          "en": "that is able to run NodeJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 201.73,
          "end": 205.4,
          "en": "And we're going to see that later in this course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.4,
          "end": 209.05,
          "en": "Now when deploying a site, an application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 209.05,
          "end": 213.73,
          "en": "you also typically need to redeploy from time to time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 213.73,
          "end": 215.78,
          "en": "And when doing a standard build,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 215.78,
          "end": 219.87,
          "en": "you need to redeploy whenever your code changes, of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 219.87,
          "end": 222.21,
          "en": "because you want your latest code to be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 222.21,
          "end": 224.6,
          "en": "in effect in production,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.6,
          "end": 228.7,
          "en": "but you will also need to redeploy if your content changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 228.7,
          "end": 232.82,
          "en": "and you need to re-render some of your pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 232.82,
          "end": 236.7,
          "en": "because you're not revalidating them on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 236.7,
          "end": 240.56,
          "en": "because you haven't added that revalidate setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 240.56,
          "end": 242.34,
          "en": "in get static props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 242.34,
          "end": 244.54,
          "en": "Then if you have such pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 244.54,
          "end": 249.22,
          "en": "as we, for example have them in our blog application here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 249.22,
          "end": 252.55,
          "en": "in our blog site, there I have pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 252.55,
          "end": 256.08,
          "en": "where I pre-rendered the pages with some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 256.08,
          "end": 258.33,
          "en": "and I don't revalidate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 258.33,
          "end": 260.97,
          "en": "If you have such pages, which is no problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 260.97,
          "end": 262.7,
          "en": "but if you have such pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 262.7,
          "end": 265.04,
          "en": "you will also need to redeploy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 265.04,
          "end": 268.58,
          "en": "whenever the contents that influences those pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 268.58,
          "end": 272.68,
          "en": "or that impacts those pages changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 272.68,
          "end": 274.3,
          "en": "Now that's the standard build,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 274.3,
          "end": 276.53,
          "en": "which you get with next build.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 276.53,
          "end": 278.4,
          "en": "For some projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 278.4,
          "end": 281.67,
          "en": "the full static build is a good option though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 281.67,
          "end": 285.953,
          "en": "You get that by running next export, another command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 286.87,
          "end": 289.11,
          "en": "We could run this in our project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 289.11,
          "end": 291.63,
          "en": "by adding a script for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 291.63,
          "end": 293.15999999999997,
          "en": "Here in package.json,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 293.15999999999997,
          "end": 295.33,
          "en": "we could add a export script",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 295.33,
          "end": 297.02,
          "en": "or a however you wanna call it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 297.02,
          "end": 299.363,
          "en": "where we then run next export.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 301.01,
          "end": 304.48,
          "en": "Now next export does something totally different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 304.48,
          "end": 306.13,
          "en": "than next build.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 306.13,
          "end": 309.94,
          "en": "It also produces an optimized production version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 309.94,
          "end": 311.35,
          "en": "of your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 311.35,
          "end": 316.12,
          "en": "but it produces a 100% static application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 316.12,
          "end": 320.5,
          "en": "which means only HTML, CSS and JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 320.5,
          "end": 322.28,
          "en": "no server-side code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 322.28,
          "end": 325.49,
          "en": "and therefore for hosting such a website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 325.49,
          "end": 328.48,
          "en": "you don't need a NodeJS server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 328.48,
          "end": 331.95,
          "en": "Which makes hosting easier because you don't need to worry",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 331.95,
          "end": 334.37,
          "en": "about scaling and so on, so much",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 334.37,
          "end": 337.52,
          "en": "because there are plenty of static hosts out there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 337.52,
          "end": 341.72,
          "en": "which scale dynamically and are very cost-effective.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 341.72,
          "end": 343.19,
          "en": "So having a static app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 343.19,
          "end": 347.15,
          "en": "which doesn't require a NodeJS server, isn't too bad.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 347.15,
          "end": 350.63,
          "en": "It can definitely make deployment a bit easier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 350.63,
          "end": 354.33,
          "en": "but next export isn't always an option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 354.33,
          "end": 358.01,
          "en": "Since it spits out a 100% steady gap,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 358.01,
          "end": 361.33,
          "en": "there are certain things, certain next features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 361.33,
          "end": 364.74,
          "en": "which you just can't use in such a application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 364.74,
          "end": 367.69,
          "en": "For example, you can't use next export",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 367.69,
          "end": 371.02,
          "en": "if your site relies on API routes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 371.02,
          "end": 374.85,
          "en": "on service-side pages with get service-side props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 374.85,
          "end": 376.97,
          "en": "on page revalidations,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 376.97,
          "end": 380.88,
          "en": "or if you have static paths with fallback set to true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 380.88,
          "end": 382.33,
          "en": "or blocking.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 382.33,
          "end": 387.18,
          "en": "All those things require a code to execute on demand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 387.18,
          "end": 390.44,
          "en": "for incoming requests on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 390.44,
          "end": 393.6,
          "en": "And therefore it's difficult, if you have no server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 393.6,
          "end": 395.88,
          "en": "So next export only works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 395.88,
          "end": 399.773,
          "en": "if you have a page which doesn't need any service-side code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 400.63,
          "end": 404.24,
          "en": "Now, when building a page with next export,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 404.24,
          "end": 406.83,
          "en": "you have to be aware of the fact that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 406.83,
          "end": 411.29,
          "en": "that means that you need to redeploy your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 411.29,
          "end": 413.29,
          "en": "whenever your code changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 413.29,
          "end": 416.63,
          "en": "but also whenever any content changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 416.63,
          "end": 419.74,
          "en": "since you can't use page revalidations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 419.74,
          "end": 421.49,
          "en": "and fallbacks and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 421.49,
          "end": 425.54,
          "en": "you need to redeploy whenever any content changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 425.54,
          "end": 428.84,
          "en": "because you'll need to export your application again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 428.84,
          "end": 431.83,
          "en": "You need to rebuild all the pages again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 431.83,
